$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 64-17-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Sonogashira Coupling Reactions. We then
investigated SiliaCat DPP-Pd, SiliaCat S-Pd, and SiliaCat Pd0 in the
heterogeneous Sonogashira coupling reactions of different iodide
substrates with phenylacetylene. Again aryl iodides with different
electron-withdrawing or -donating groups and different heteroatoms were
tested (Scheme 3). Remarkably, the presence of a cocatalyst was not
required. Results in Table 6 show that in general yields are high for all
catalysts. Only substrate 2-iodo-aniline (entry 8) could not be fully
coupled with phenylacetylene. However, SiliaCat Pd0 is the most selective
catalyst with minimum 94% selectivity in the conversion of 2-iodo-phenol
(entry 6). Table 6, entry 4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported catalyst, Sonogashira coupling, alternative reaction
conditions gave lower conversion or selectivity, alternative reaction
conditions shown, miniblock synthesizer used, diphenylphosphine-based
catalyst on silica, selective reaction, 100% selectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Screening and Library Generation in Parallel C-C Coupling
Reactions Mediated by Organosilica SiliaCat Palladium Catalysts
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pandarus, Valerica; Gingras, Genevieve; Beland, Francois; Ciriminna,
Rosaria; Pagliaro, Mario
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Process Research & Development (2012), 16(1), 117-122

