$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Sonogashira Coupling Reactions. We then investigated SiliaCat DPP-Pd,
SiliaCat S-Pd, and SiliaCat Pd0 in the heterogeneous Sonogashira coupling
reactions of different iodide substrates with phenylacetylene. Again aryl
iodides with different electron-withdrawing or -donating groups and
different heteroatoms were tested (Scheme 3). Remarkably, the presence of
a cocatalyst was not required. Results in Table 6 show that in general
yields are high for all catalysts. Only substrate 2-iodo-aniline (entry
8) could not be fully coupled with phenylacetylene. However, SiliaCat Pd0
is the most selective catalyst with minimum 94% selectivity in the
conversion of 2-iodo-phenol (entry 6). Table 6, entry 1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported catalyst, Sonogashira coupling, alternative reaction
conditions shown, alternative reaction conditions gave the same
conversion and selectivity, miniblock synthesizer used,
diphenylphosphine-based catalyst on silica, selective reaction, 100%
selectivity
