and Et3N (5 mL) were added to
1-[2-deoxy-3,5-di-O-(p-toluoyl)-β-D-erythro-pentofuranosyl]-5-iodouracil
(900 mg, 1.59 mmol) in a 30-mL flask equipped with a Teflon valve, and N2
was bubbled through the stirred solution for 10 min. Addition of 13a (254
mg, 1.60 mmol) was followed by (Ph3P)4Pd (72 mg, 0.06 mmol) and CuI (19
mg, 0.08 mmol), and stirring was continued for 1.5 h at 50 °C. Volatiles
were evaporated, and the residue was chromatographed (EtOAc/hexanes, 1:2
→ EtOAc) to give 14a (745 mg, 97%).
1-[2-Deoxy-3,5-di-O-(p-toluoyl)-β-D-erythro-pentofuranosyl]-5-[2-(5-hexylpyrid-2-yl)ethynyl]uracil
(14c). 1H NMR δ 0.88 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H), 1.26-1.38 (m, 6H), 1.56-1.65
(m, 2H), 2.25, 2.43 (2. s, 2. 3H), 2.30-2.36 (m, 1H), 2.59 (t, J = 7.8
Hz, 2H), 2.77 (dd, J = 5.4, 14.2 Hz, 1H), 4.56-4.58 (m, 1H), 4.65, 4.80
(2. dd, J = 3.4, 12.2 Hz, 2. 1H), 5.60 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 1H), 6.39 (dd, J =
5.9, 8.8 Hz, 1H), 7.15-7.30 (m, 5H), 7.43 (dd, J = 2.0, 7.8 Hz, 1H),
7.91-7.94 (m, 4H), 8.06 (s, 1H), 8.41 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 8.99 (br s,
1H); 13C NMR δ 14.0, 21.5, 21.6, 22.5, 28.7, 30.8, 31.5, 32.8, 38.3,
64.1, 74.8, 79.6, 83.1, 85.8, 92.7, 100.2, 126.2 (2C), 126.3, 126.8,
129.2, 129.4, 129.5, 129.7, 135.7, 137.7, 139.9, 142.5, 144.1, 144.4,
149.3, 150.0, 161.0, 165.8, 166.1; FAB-MS m/z 650 ([M + H+], 50%), 298
(100%); HRMS m/z 650.2858 (M + H+ [C38H40N3O7] = 650.2866).
