$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure A for the synthesis of
compounds 7a-p. Compound 6 (1 eq), aryl acetylene (5 eq.), Pd(PPh3)4 (2
mol %), Amberlite IR-67 (5 eq.) and CuI (20 mol %) in THF was heated for
15 min at 120 °C in the microwave. After cooling to ambient temperature,
the reaction mixture was filtered through a pad of Celite. The solvent
was removed in vacuo and the crude product was purified by flash column
chromatography on silica gel. Compound 4 (0.20 g, 0.66 mmol) was
converted to the target compound using general procedure A. The crude
product was purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel (MeOH :
CHCl3 = 1 : 30).
3-(3,3-dimethylbut-1-ynyl)-1-isopropyl-1H-pyrazolo[3,4-d]pyrimidin-4-amine
(7o): Compound 6 (0.15 g, 0.50 mmol) was converted to the target compound
using general procedure A. The crude product was purified by flash column
chromatography on silica gel (MeOH : CHCl3 = 1 : 20) yielding 7o (97%) as
a white powder. 1H NMR (400 MHz, d6-DMSO): δ 8.21 (s, 1H), 4.98 (sept, J
6.6 Hz, 1H), 1.42 (d, J 6.6 Hz, 6H), 1.35 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 158.0, 155.8, 152.0, 103.6, 101.8, 77.2, 71.5, 49.1, 30.5,
28.2, 21.8. HRMS [M+1]+ calculated for C14H20N5+: 258.1713; found
258.1719. HRMS [M+1]+ calculated for C14H20N5+: 258.1713; found 258.1706.
Anal. Calc. for C14H19N5: C, 65.34; H, 7.44; N, 27.22. Found: C, 65.26;
H, 7.44; N, 27.22.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, microwave irradiation, Amberlite IR-67 used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of
3-Substituted-1-Isopropyl-1H-pyrazolo[3,4-d]pyrimidin-4-amines as RET
Kinase Inhibitors
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Diner, Peter; Alao, John P.; Soederlund, Johan; Sunnerhagen, Per;
Groetli, Morten
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
