$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM tert-Butyl-3-((trimethylsilyl)ethynyl)benzylcarbamate (10) To a stirred
suspension of tert-butyl-3-iodobenzylcarbamate (590 mg, 1.77 mmol), CuI
(33.7 mg, 0.177 mmol) and PdCl2(PPh3)2 (62.1 mg, 0.090 mmol) in THF (17.7
mL) was added Et3N (493 μL, 3.54 mmol) followed by
trimethylsilylacetylene (302 μL, 2.13 mmol). The reaction was heated to
100 °C, under microwave irradiation, for 20 min. Once cooled the
resulting suspension was filtered and the filtrate concentrated in vacuo
to give a crude brown oil (900 mg). Purification was accomplished by
flash chromatography on silica gel eluting with EtOAc/hexane (10%), The
title compound (510 mg, 95%) as an orange/brown solid. 1H-NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) 0.25 (s, 9H, -Si(CH3)3), 1.46 (s, 9H, -C(CH3)3), 4.28 (d, J = 4.8
Hz, 2H,-CH2-), 4.83 (br s, 1H, -NH-), 7.22 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H, CHar),
7.25 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H, CHar), 7.35 (dt, J = 7.4, 1.5 Hz, 1H, CHar),
7.38 (s, 1H, CHar); LC-MS (ESI, m/z): Rt = 2.94 min -326 (M + Na)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Sonogashira coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
