$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-Phenethyl-3-(2-(phenylethynyl)phenyl)propanamide (17).
3-(2-Bromophenyl)-N-phenethylpropanamide 16 (0.51 g, 1.53 mmol) was
dissolved in triethylamine (15 mL) and DME (15 mL). PdCl2(PPh3)2 (0.035
g, 0.046 mmol), copper (I) iodide (0.02 g, 0.1 mmol), and phenylacetylene
(0.17 mL, 1.5 mmol) were added, and the solution was heated at 120 °C for
16 h with stirring. The reaction mixture was evaporated under reduced
pressure, and the residue was dissolved in ethyl acetate and filtered.
The filtrate was washed with saturated aqueous brine solution and dried
over MgSO4. The residue was purified using silica scavenger 2, at which
point the palladium content was measured by ICPOES. Further purification
by column chromatography using gradient elution from 0.5% to 60% ethyl
acetate/hexane gave17 (0.53 g, 93%). 1H NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.48-
7.42 (m, 2H), 7.31-7.26 (m, 2H), 7.21-7.11 (m, 7H), 7.03- 6.95 (m, 3H),
3.43-3.33 (m, 2H), 3.11 (t, J = 7.11 Hz, 1H), 3.01-2.95 (m, 1H),
2.70-2.58 (m, 2H), 2.49-2.43 (m, 1H), 2.38-2.32 (m, 1H); MS (ES+): m/z =
354 [M + H]+, m/z = 376 ) [M + Na]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Sonogashira coupling 1st step, supported reagent 2nd step, without
scavenging of Pd (2nd step) Pd 700 ppm, isolated product after scavenging
5 ppm Pd
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly Functionalized Sulfur-Based Silica Scavengers for the Efficient
Removal of Palladium Species from Active Pharmaceutical Ingredients
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Galaffu, Nicola; Man, Siud Pui; Wilkes, Robin D.; Wilson, John R. H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Process Research & Development (2007), 11(3), 406-413

