$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Sonogashira Coupling 25. Ethyl ester HCl salt 22 (33.5g × 96 wt % = 32.2
g, 56.9 mmol), alkyne linker acid 24 DCHA salt (40.1 g, 80 mmol),
allylpalladium chloride dimer (0.35 g, 0.95 mmol), and
tritert-butylphosphine HBF4 (1.13 g, 3.9 mmol) were slurried in
acetonitrile (263 g). The contents were sparged with nitrogen for 20 min,
then diisopropylamine (DIPA, 32.2 g, 318 mmol) was charged, and the
mixture was sparged for another 15 min. The batch was heated to 50 °C,
aged for 1 h until HPLC indicated complete reaction, and then cooled to 0
°C. The batch was then treated with trifluoroacetic acid (TFA) (40.5 g)
at <60 °C. The batch was seeded, cooled to 20 °C over 3 h, and aged at 20
°C for 18 h. The product was isolated via filtration and the wet cake
washed with acetonitrile (55 g). The solid was dried in a vacuum oven at
50 °C. The title compound, 56.7 g, 67 wt %, the remaining mass was
DIPA-TFA salt. (90% yield). 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6): δ 8.06 (d, J =
8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.91 (t, J = 5.5 Hz, 1H), 7.36-7.24 (om, 7H), 5.66 (br s,
1H), 5.11-4.96 (om, 2H), 4.60 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 0.5H), 4.54 (t, J = 7.7 Hz,
0.5H), 4.13 (q, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 4.03 (q, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 3.92 (s, 3H),
3.92-3.76 (om, 5H), 3.3 (m, 0.6H), 3.08 (m, 2.4H), 2.66 (m, 1H),
2.49-2.42 (om, 2H), 2.35 (m, 1H), 1.97 (m, 5H), 1.73 (m, 5H), 1.65-1.54
(om, 9H), 1.32-1.17 (om, 14H), 1.14-1.02 (om, 15H).). 13C NMR (125 MHz,
9:1 DMSO-d 6:CD3OD, mixture of rotamers): δ 173.43, 172.46, 172.06,
160.84, 158.49, 158.47, 156.89, 154.52, 154.07, 140.89, 139.33, 137.04,
136.80, 128.54, 128.51, 128.46, 128.43, 120.02, 127.98, 127.52, 127.41,
115.01, 114.98, 113.50, 104.86, 93.46, 78.39, 74.16, 73.47, 71.03, 66.66,
66.46, 61.08, 60.99, 59.09, 58.29, 57.86, 56.15, 52.82, 52.51, 52.44,
52.33, 46.56, 40.32, 36.30, 35.30, 35.06, 29.46, 29.39, 29.01, 28.31,
25.89, 25.83, 25.02, 24.15, 23.79, 23.75, 18.76, 14.06, 13.94. HRMS calcd
for C41H49N3O10 744.3496, found 744.3511 (M + 1).
